=== STAGE 0b: Analysis of the SKIPPED Stages from check.sh

The local Windows developer run reports 'check: PASSED WITH 3 SKIPPED (skips are not passes - install the missing tools for full coverage)'.
The 3 counted skips are external Linux-only tools absent from the Windows developer host (installed and required to pass in CI on ubuntu-latest):
  1. Stage 7 / oracle-disk.py: 'SKIP  sgdisk not found' (GPT oracle requires sgdisk from gdisk package; installed in CI).
  2. Stage 7 / oracle-disk.py: 'SKIP  fsck.fat not found' (FAT oracle requires fsck.fat from dosfstools package; installed in CI).
  3. Stage 7 / oracle-disk.py: 'SKIP  mdir not found' (directory oracle requires mdir from mtools package; installed in CI).

Additional notices for absent tools in Stage 9:
  - Stage 9 / check.sh: 'SKIP: fsck.fat not installed (install: apt-get install dosfstools)' (FAT32 corpus validation; installed in CI).
  - Stage 9 / check.sh: 'SKIP: mdir not installed (install: apt-get install mtools)' (corpus directory listing diff against kernel FATLIST; installed in CI).

Additional internal harness skips:
  - novacore/tests/test_llm_privacy.py: test_prompt_file_and_dir_permissions_posix skipped on Windows ('POSIX file permission bits only').
  - kernel/src/excselftest.rs: #XM SSE 0/0 unmasked skipped in QEMU TCG mode (qemu#215; delivered on KVM / real HW).

